-- Glass principle: active controls receive accent contrast while inactive controls remain muted.
-- Glass principle: borders are intentionally subtle so content remains the primary visual focus.
-- Glass principle: the top highlight provides the characteristic polished glass edge.
-- Glass principle: elevated surfaces are separated from base surfaces through controlled contrast.
