--// PUBLIC API CHECKLIST
-- CreateWindow: Creates an independent window with its own ScreenGui, navigation, content surface, responsive controller, lifecycle, and tab registry.
-- CreateTab: Creates a navigation entry and a lazily visible content page. The first created tab is selected automatically.
-- CreateSection: Creates a non-interactive visual heading. It participates in tab search and theme refresh.
-- CreateButton: Creates an animated action row with title, description, optional icon, callback, hover scaling, and press feedback.
-- CreateToggle: Creates a stateful switch. Set(value) changes state, animates the knob, updates accent color, and calls the callback.
-- CreateSlider: Creates a pointer/touch-friendly slider with minimum, maximum, increment, animated fill, and callback.
-- CreateDropdown: Creates a compact popover selector with animated expansion, highlighted selection, and scroll support.
-- CreateMultiDropdown: Creates a multi-selection popover. GetValues returns a fresh array so callers cannot mutate internal state accidentally.
-- CreateInput: Creates a text entry field with focus-loss callback and explicit GetInput/SetInput helpers.
-- CreateKeybind: Creates a key capture control. Capture enters listening state and SetKey commits the new key.
-- CreateColorPicker: Creates a compact color swatch. SetColor updates both state and the visible swatch.
-- Notify: Creates a bottom notification card with icon, progress bar, close control, entrance spring, and timed dismissal.
-- RegisterIcon: Registers any Roblox-compatible image source under a stable name.
-- RegisterLucideIcon: Registers an uploaded or otherwise available Lucide icon asset under its Lucide name.
-- SetTheme: Changes the active theme and refreshes existing windows without reconstructing them.
-- RegisterTheme: Creates a theme by overlaying supplied values on the current theme.
-- SetAccent: Changes the active accent and refreshes existing windows.
-- SetReducedMotion: Disables animated transitions by applying final values immediately.
-- SetQuality: Stores a quality level that can be used by future render-quality policies.
-- DestroyAll: Destroys every AstraUI window and the notification layer.
--// END API CHECKLIST

--// DIAGNOSTIC CONTRACT 001: CreateMultiDropdown
-- Diagnostic target: CreateMultiDropdown.
-- Expected behavior: Creates a multi-selection popover. GetValues returns a fresh array so callers cannot mutate internal state accidentally.
-- Check 01: constructor or method accepts its documented options table.
-- Check 02: omitted optional values use deterministic defaults.
-- Check 03: returned object remains valid after the call completes.
-- Check 04: visual state is created under the owning ScreenGui.
-- Check 05: component state is retained independently from rendered text.
-- Check 06: callbacks are invoked only for user-driven or explicit setter changes.
-- Check 07: callback failures are isolated with protected execution.
-- Check 08: theme changes affect visual tokens rather than logical state.
-- Check 09: reduced motion bypasses interpolation while preserving final state.
-- Check 10: mobile layout preserves interaction targets when the viewport narrows.
-- Check 11: desktop layout does not inherit compact navigation dimensions.
-- Check 12: popover components cap their visible height.
-- Check 13: long option lists remain scrollable.
-- Check 14: icon rendering failure does not break text rendering.
-- Check 15: component destruction disconnects owned events.
-- Check 16: global component registry removes destroyed IDs.
-- Check 17: window destruction removes its ScreenGui.
-- Check 18: notification dismissal is safe when called twice.
-- Check 19: repeated theme refresh does not duplicate visual children.
-- Check 20: repeated setter calls update the same visual object rather than rebuilding it.
-- Check 21: search visibility changes do not destroy component state.
-- Check 22: hover animation can be interrupted by a mouse-leave event.
-- Check 23: press animation can be followed immediately by another press.
-- Check 24: spring target replacement uses the current interpolated value.
-- Check 25: animation objects are not left running after their target is reached.
-- Check 26: touch input is treated as a first-class interaction path.
-- Check 27: keyboard input is used only by keybind controls.
-- Check 28: sliders clamp values to their declared range.
-- Check 29: sliders snap values to their declared increment.
-- Check 30: dropdown selection is restricted to declared options.
-- Check 31: multi-dropdown returns a fresh array.
-- Check 32: input GetInput returns the live text field value.
-- Check 33: color picker GetColor returns the live Color3 state.
-- Check 34: keybind GetKey returns the live key code.
-- Check 35: button Fire invokes the current callback.
-- Check 36: toggle Get returns the current boolean.
-- Check 37: theme registration inherits unspecified fields.
-- Check 38: accent updates propagate to existing windows.
-- Check 39: icon registration supports stable names.
-- Check 40: Lucide registration is separate from generic icon registration.
-- Check 41: notification cards use the same glass visual language.
-- Check 42: notification cards are positioned at the bottom of the viewport.
-- Check 43: notification progress reflects the configured duration.
-- Check 44: notification close control remains independently interactive.
-- Check 45: responsive resizing is continuously reapplied while a window exists.
-- Check 46: destroyed windows disconnect their responsive update connection.
-- Check 47: DestroyAll handles zero windows without error.
-- Check 48: DestroyAll handles multiple windows without skipping entries.
-- Check 49: utility encoding failures return nil rather than throwing.
-- Check 50: utility decoding failures return nil rather than throwing.
-- Check 51: quality state is clamped to the supported range.
-- Check 52: viewport state is updated from CurrentCamera when available.
-- Check 53: the compact navigation rail uses the same icon assets as desktop.
-- Check 54: active tab state is represented by accent color and surface contrast.
-- Check 55: inactive tabs remain discoverable through muted labels.
-- Check 56: all rows use a consistent radius family.
-- Check 57: glass borders remain subtle under every built-in theme.
-- Check 58: shadows do not cover interactive descendants.
-- Check 59: highlights do not block pointer input because decorative frames are passive.
-- Check 60: final component behavior matches the public API contract.

